@startuml mtga-architecture
title MTGA Companion - Target System Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor Player

node "User device - private trust boundary" as Device {
  component "Wails frontend\nTypeScript" as Frontend
  component "Local backend\nGo modular monolith" as Local
  database "SQLite\ncollections, decks, graph runs, outbox" as SQLite
  file "MTGA Detailed Logs\nread-only preferred source" as Logs
  component "Python exporter\nlegacy fallback" as Legacy
  component "MTGA process memory\nlegacy read-only source" as Memory
}

cloud "Central platform" as Central {
  component "HTTPS API\nGo, stateless" as API
  component "Catalog worker" as CatalogWorker
  component "Telemetry ingest\nopt-in, aggregate" as Telemetry
  database "PostgreSQL\nmetadata and aggregate metrics" as ProdPG
  storage "Object storage / CDN\nversioned catalog snapshots" as Objects
  component "Authenticated operations" as Operations
}

cloud "Approved data providers" as Providers
cloud "Optional model provider" as Model

node "Development boundary - never shipped" as Development {
  component "Development MCP\nstdio, read-only by default" as DevMCP
  component "Contract, load and fault tests" as Tests
  database "PostgreSQL\ndev / staging only" as DevPG
  database "SQLite fixtures" as FixtureDB
}

Player --> Frontend
Frontend --> Local : typed Wails bindings
Local --> Frontend : progress and result events
Local --> Logs : tail and parse
Legacy --> Memory : compatibility scan
Local ..> Legacy : explicit fallback
Local <--> SQLite : local transactions
Local --> API : HTTPS; manifest and opt-in batches
Local --> Objects : catalog by version and hash
Local ..> Model : minimal approved context
Providers --> CatalogWorker : scheduled import
CatalogWorker --> ProdPG : normalized metadata
CatalogWorker --> Objects : immutable snapshot
API --> Telemetry : validated event batches
Telemetry --> ProdPG : aggregate writes
Operations --> ProdPG : audited privileged access
DevMCP --> DevPG : restricted development role
DevMCP --> FixtureDB : inspect graph and event fixtures
DevMCP --> API : dev/staging diagnostics only
Tests --> Frontend
Tests --> Local
Tests --> API
Tests --> DevPG

note bottom of Device
  Raw logs, collection contents and local paths stay on the device.
  SQLite is the product source of truth; exports are projections.
end note
note bottom of Development
  Reject production DSNs. No product packaging and no runtime dependency.
end note
@enduml
